{"@context":{"iri":"@id","prefLabel":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel","altLabels":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel","definition":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition","notation":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation","broader":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader","scheme":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme","schemeLabel":"https://prez.dev/schemeLabel"},"@graph":[{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/acousticPorosity","prefLabel":"acoustic porosity","altLabels":["acoustic borehole logging"],"definition":"Porosity determined by acoustic logging as a function of the difference in acoustic travel time between interstitial fluids and the rock matrix","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/airPermeability","prefLabel":"air permeability","definition":"Permeability measured with air","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/permeability","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/apparentGrainDensity","prefLabel":"apparent grain density","definition":"Grain density calculated by an unknown method","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/apparentMassDensity","prefLabel":"apparent mass density","altLabels":["bagged mass density"],"definition":"Apparent mass density determined by a vacuum bagging method","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/apparentPorosity","prefLabel":"apparent porosity","altLabels":["water absorption"],"definition":"Apparent porosity is the ratio of interconnected void spaces only, is derived determining the fluid volume of interconnecting pores and dividing by the bulk volume. This may be performed by gravimetry using water or gas pycnometry.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/boundWaterContent","prefLabel":"bound water content","definition":"Water in the pore space that does not flow under normal reservoir conditions. When used in connection with a nuclear magnetic resonance measurement, the term refers to all the water that is not free to move. This includes capillary-bound water and clay-bound water.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/waterContent","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/caliper","prefLabel":"caliper","altLabels":["borehole diameter"],"definition":"Borehole internal diameter (caliper) associated with gamma-gamma density borehole tools, units in mm","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/capillaryBoundWaterContent","prefLabel":"capillary-bound water content","definition":"Water that is not free to move due to capillary tension. When used to describe NMR results, capillary-bound water is defined as the water signal between certain cutoffs, typically above 3 ms and below 33 ms.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/waterContent","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/chargeability","prefLabel":"chargeability","definition":"Chargeability is the ability of the Earth to hold a direct current (DC) charge, with decay time measured in milliseconds (ms). This is most commonly measured using time-domain induced polarization (IP) equipment.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/clayBoundWaterContent","prefLabel":"clay-bound water content","definition":"Water that is not free to move due to being bound to clays. When used to describe NMR results, clay-bound water is defined as the water signal below a certain cutoff, typically 3 ms.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/waterContent","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/deltaT","prefLabel":"delta T","altLabels":["Delta T"],"definition":"The difference of temperature between two measuring points. The temperature differs either in time and/or position. Differential temperature is expressed in Kelvin. No matter if the value is measured in °Celsius or in Fahrenheit. Therefore the values can be compared easily. The units are expressed in Kelvin(K) The lowest temperature is 0 K. No negative numbers exist in the Kelvin scale.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/densityPorosity","prefLabel":"density porosity","altLabels":["gamma density porosity","gamma porosity"],"definition":"Density porosity is determined by emission of gamma-rays into the borehole wall and measurement of their interaction. Density porosity is then derived using other data to inform on the rock matrix density","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/dryBulkMassDensity","prefLabel":"dry bulk mass density","altLabels":["dry bulk density","particle density on a dry basis"],"definition":"Ratio of the dry rock mass to the total volumes of the rock material and pores (ie, the bulk volume of the sample).","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/dynamicBulkModulus","prefLabel":"Dynamic Bulk Modulus","altLabels":["K"],"definition":"Dynamic Bulk Modulus calculated from laboratory measured ultrasonic properties","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/dynamicPoissonsRatio","prefLabel":"Dynamic Poisson's Ratio","altLabels":["v"],"definition":"Dynamic Poisson's Ratio calculated from laboratory measured ultrasonic properties","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/poissonsRatio","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/dynamicShearModulus","prefLabel":"Dynamic Shear Modulus","altLabels":["G"],"definition":"Dynamic Shear Modulus","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/dynamicYoungsModulus","prefLabel":"Dynamic Young's Modulus","altLabels":["E"],"definition":"Dynamic Young's Modulus calculated from laboratory measured ultrasonic properties","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/youngsModulus","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/electricalConductivity","prefLabel":"electrical conductivity","altLabels":["specific conductance"],"definition":"The ability of a rock mass to conduct an electrical current, determined by electromagnetic induction","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/electricalPotential","prefLabel":"electrical potential","definition":"The spontaneous potential probe measures the differences in natural electrical potential between the surface electrode and an electrode in the drillhole, and so measures the differences in natural electrical potential between the drillhole fluid and the surrounding rock material. The spontaneous potential log is used to determine bed thicknesses, the nature of the formations, identify porous and permeable beds and indicate the salinity of the groundwater in the formation.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/electricalResistance","prefLabel":"electrical resistance","definition":"resistance between two points, measuring resistivity of different lithological units","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/electricalResistivity","prefLabel":"electrical resistivity","altLabels":["resistivity"],"definition":"The ability of a rock volume to impede an electrical current","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/freeWaterContent","prefLabel":"free water content","altLabels":["mobile water content"],"definition":"Water that is mobile, available to flow, and not bound to surfaces of grains or minerals in rock. When used in connection with nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) measurements, free water is all the water that is not clay bound, capillary bound or in mineral hydrates.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/waterContent","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaBulkDensity","prefLabel":"gamma bulk density","altLabels":["RHOB","gamma-gamma"],"definition":"Bulk density (combined minerals and pore fluids) derived using a bore hole gamma bulk density tool","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaDifferentialDensity","prefLabel":"gamma differential density","altLabels":["DRHOB"],"definition":"Incremental change in bulk density measured by a bore hole gamma density tool","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaBulkDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaLongSpacedDensity","prefLabel":"gamma long spaced density","altLabels":["LSD"],"definition":"Bulk density determined by a bore hole long spaced gamma density tool","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaBulkDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaShortSpacedDensity","prefLabel":"gamma short spaced density","altLabels":["HRD","SSD"],"definition":"Bulk density determined by a bore hole short-spaced gamma density tool. Also referred to as high resolution density.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gammaBulkDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/gasPermeability","prefLabel":"gas permeability","definition":"Gas Permeability measure of ultra low permeability samples that are below limit of detection for standard poroperm tests","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/permeability","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/grainMassDensity","prefLabel":"grain mass density","altLabels":["apparent particle d","grain density","matrix density"],"definition":"The density of a rock or mineral with no porosity, also known as matrix density, commonly in units of g/cm3.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/heatFlow","prefLabel":"heat flow","altLabels":["Q"],"definition":"The rate at which a rock mass conducts heat","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/heatProduction","prefLabel":"heat production","definition":"Calculated heat production of a rock derived from its K, Th and U radioisotopic composition, density and age","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/hydraulicConductivity","prefLabel":"hydraulic conductivity","definition":"The capacity of a rock to transmit water","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/indirectTensileStrength","prefLabel":"indirect tensile strength","definition":"Indirect tensile strength","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/K","prefLabel":"K","altLabels":["POTA","potassium"],"definition":"Potassium abundance measured by a spectral gamma-ray emission spectrometric method","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/naturalGamma","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/koenigsbergerRatio","prefLabel":"Koenigsberger ratio","altLabels":["Q ratio"],"definition":"The Koenigsberger ratio (Q ratio) is defined as the ratio in a rock of remanent magnetization to the induced magnetization in the Earth's field. Q = NRM (in A/m) / (K (in SI) * H (in A/m), where K is the magnetic susceptibility in SI units and H is the local geomagnetic field (generally based on the International Geomagnetic Reference Field value at the sample site and at the sampling date).","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/magneticSusceptibility","prefLabel":"magnetic susceptibility","altLabels":["MS","magsus"],"definition":"The degree to which a material can be magnetized in an external magnetic field, measured a dimensionless proportionality constant.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","prefLabel":"mass density","altLabels":["density"],"definition":"\"Density\" as a generic description is the mass per unit volume of a material where a more accurate description, or the method of determination (e.g. dry bulk, wet bulk, grain ) is not given.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/meanLogT2","prefLabel":"mean log T2","altLabels":["mlT2"],"definition":"The geometric mean of the T2 NMR distribution. T2 is the transverse (or spin-spin) relaxation time.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrRelaxation","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/naturalGamma","prefLabel":"natural gamma","altLabels":["GRDE"],"definition":"A measure of the natural gamma-ray emission of a material, related to the radioelements K, Th and U and/or their daughter products.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/neutronPorosity","prefLabel":"neutron porosity","definition":"Neutron porosity is determined by measuring the ability of wall rocks to slow fast neutrons to the slow thermal neutron state. The number of thermal neutrons created is proportional to the amount of hydrogen present, in the form of oil or water, in pore","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrClayBoundWaterPorosity","prefLabel":"NMR clay-bound water porosity","altLabels":["MCBW"],"definition":"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Porosity is determined by  measuring the relaxation of hydrogen nuclei after alignment by the strong magnetic field generated by the NMR tool. Values may include Effective Porosity (MPHI), Total Porosity (MSIG) and Clay-Bound Water Porosity (MCBW), normally quoted as MSIG","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrEffectivePorosity","prefLabel":"NMR effective porosity","altLabels":["MPHI"],"definition":"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Porosity is determined by  measuring the relaxation of hydrogen nuclei after alignment by the strong magnetic field generated by the NMR tool. Values may include Effective Porosity (MPHI), Total Porosity (MSIG) and Clay-Bound Water Porosity (MCBW), normally quoted as MSIG","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrRelaxation","prefLabel":"NMR relaxation","definition":"The decay characteristics of signals emitted in a polarising field by populations of certain atomic nuclei following removal of an external magnetic field.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrTotalPorosity","prefLabel":"NMR total porosity","altLabels":["MSIG"],"definition":"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Porosity is determined by  measuring the relaxation of hydrogen nuclei after alignment by the strong magnetic field generated by the NMR tool. Values may include Effective Porosity (MPHI), Total Porosity (MSIG) and Clay-Bound Water Porosity (MCBW), normally quoted as MSIG","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/pWaveAxialVelocity","prefLabel":"P-wave axial velocity","definition":"P-wave velocity of a rock core measured parallel to the core axis","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/pWaveSlowness","prefLabel":"P-wave slowness","definition":"P-Wave slowness measured at a single stress point during Unconfined Compressive Strength testing","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/pWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"P-wave velocity","altLabels":["Vp"],"definition":"P-Wave velocity measured at a single stress point during Unconfined Compressive Strength testing","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/permeability","prefLabel":"permeability","altLabels":["fluid flow"],"definition":"A measure of the ability of a fluid to flow through a material. Units are normally expressed as darcy or millidarcy, but can also be expressed as the SI unit m^2 or cm^2","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/permeabilityKlinkenbergCorrected","prefLabel":"permeability (Klinkenberg corrected)","definition":"Klinkenberg correction is applied to reduce air permeability to an equivalent liquid permeability","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/permeability","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/poissonsRatio","prefLabel":"Poisson's Ratio","definition":"Poisson's Ratio","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","prefLabel":"porosity","definition":"Porosity is the ratio of pore spaces to rock volume. May be determined as either total or apparent porosity.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/remanentMagnetisation","prefLabel":"remanent magnetisation","altLabels":["NRM","RM"],"definition":"Remanent magnetisation (here assumed to be the natural remanent magnetisation) is the permanent magnetisation of a rock material, attained over the material's lifetime.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sWaveAxialVelocity","prefLabel":"S-wave axial velocity","definition":"First arrival S-wave velocity measured parallel to core axis","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sWaveSlowness","prefLabel":"S-wave slowness","definition":"S-Wave slowness measured at a single stress point during Unconfined Compressive Strength testing","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"S-wave velocity","altLabels":["Vs"],"definition":"S-Wave velocity measured at a single stress point during Unconfined Compressive Strength testing","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","prefLabel":"sonic velocity","altLabels":["acoustic velocity"],"definition":"Generic velocity of sound in rock, P- or S-wave unknown","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/strikeParallelRadialPWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"strike-parallel radial P-wave velocity","altLabels":["Radial sonic velocity"],"definition":"P-wave velocity measured perpendicular to the core axis (radial), parallel to foliation strike","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/strikeParallelSWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"strike-parallel radial S-wave velocity","altLabels":["Radial S-wave velocity"],"definition":"First arrival S-wave velocity measured perpendicular to core axis (radial), parallel to foliation strike","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/strikePerpendicularPWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"strike-perpendicular radial P-wave velocity","altLabels":["Perpendicular radial sonic velocity"],"definition":"P-wave velocity, measured perpendicular to core axis (radial), perpendicular to foliation strike","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/strikePerpendicularRadialSWaveVelocity","prefLabel":"strike-perpendicular radial S-wave velocity","altLabels":["Perpendicular radial S-wave velocity"],"definition":"First arrival S-wave velocity, measured perpendicular to core axis (radial), perpendicular to foliation strike","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/sonicVelocity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/T2star","prefLabel":"T-2-star","altLabels":["FID","Free Induction Decay"],"definition":"The FID (Free Induction Decay) is the transient NMR signal resulting from the stimulation of the nuclei at the Larmor frequency. The characteristic time constant for a FID signal decay is called T2* (T-two-star).","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrRelaxation","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/T1","prefLabel":"T1","altLabels":["longitudinal NMR relaxation time"],"definition":"The longitudinal (spin-lattice) relaxation time, the decay constant for the recovery of the z component of the nuclear spin magnetisation towards its thermal equilibrium value.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrRelaxation","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/T2","prefLabel":"T2","definition":"The time it takes for the magnetic resonance signal to irreversibly decay to 37% (1/e) of its initial value after its generation by tipping the longitudinal magnetisation towards the magnetic transverse plane.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/nmrRelaxation","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","prefLabel":"temperature","definition":"The temperature of bore hole wall rocks as measure using a bore hole temperature probe","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/Th","prefLabel":"Th","altLabels":["THOR","thorium"],"definition":"Thorium abundance measured by a spectral gamma-ray emission spectrometric method","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/naturalGamma","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/thermalAnisotropy","prefLabel":"thermal anisotropy","definition":"The directional dependance of heat flow in a rock mass","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/thermalConductivity","prefLabel":"thermal conductivity","altLabels":["k","k-value (US)","lamda","lamda-value (Europe)"],"definition":"A material's ability to conduct heat","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/temperature","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/thinSectionPorosity","prefLabel":"thin section porosity","definition":"Porosity determined by automated optical scanning or point-counting methods on thin-sectioned material","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/totalPorosity","prefLabel":"total porosity","definition":"Total porosity is the ratio of sealed-off and interconnected pores to rock volume, is derived from the excess of the bulk volume over grain volume as part of Archimedes density determinations. This may be performed by gravimetry using water or gas pycnometry.","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/porosity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/U","prefLabel":"U","altLabels":["URA","uranium"],"definition":"Uranium abundance measured by a spectral gamma-ray emission spectrometric method","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/naturalGamma","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/unconfinedCompressiveStrength","prefLabel":"unconfined compressive strength","altLabels":["UCS"],"definition":"Unconfined compressive strength","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/waterContent","prefLabel":"water content","definition":"The amount of water contained in a geologic material such as soil, sediments, or rock.","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/wetBulkMassDensity","prefLabel":"wet bulk mass density","altLabels":["in situ bulk density","particloe dr","saturated","wet"],"definition":"The saturated density of a sample. The saturating fluid may be water (determine density by gravimetry in water) or a gas (determine density by gas pycnometry).","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/xctAverageBulkDensity","prefLabel":"XCT average bulk density","definition":"Rock bulk density as measured by XCT scanner","broader":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/massDensity","scheme":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty","schemeLabel":"Geology Rock Properties - Petrophysical"},{"iri":"https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/PetrophysicalProperty/xctTotalPorosity","prefLabel":"XCT total porosity","altLabels":["X-Ray tomography porosity"],"definition":"Computed (X-ray) tomography porosity is derived in the laboratory using X-ray tomography (XCT) to measure mineral grains, saturated and unsaturated pore spaces in 